I still have disk copies for Whitesmiths C somewhere and the black bound 
manual is still in a bookcase. I used it at Racal in the late 80's 
writing s/ware for the Planet network. The version we bought was a cross 
compiler from dos to pdp11. All the Planet s/w at the time was written 
in macro, under 11/34's running rsx and the whitesmiths C was an attempt 
to move development over to pc's. The 11/34's we used had 4 RL01's per 
machine, running rsx and could support 6 or more users doing edits. 
However, once a task build started for Planet, you couldn't get into the 
machine for hours :-). Processor target was a qbus Falcon embedded pdp 
board, which was the system controller for the network.

Did some good work there, with good people, though the site was 
eventually shut down and a lot of the redundant dec kit scrapped or 
given away to the employees. Yet another example of a great British 
company gone to the dogs...

Regards,

Chris


